Decision r002 — after source/metadata screening, before selecting new measurement outcomes

Bounded searches were executed through EuropePMC, not an inferred browser cache: discovery-{nuclear-receptor,mtor,qki,hormone}.json plus two TITLE_ABS refinements. Initial broad full-text searches were noisy and first-page-limited; refinements had 135 mTOR and 114 LXR/progesterone hits, not an exhausted corpus. The hand-authored browser ledger initially described planned routes as executed; it is corrected to zero such requests, and no claim relies on it. Actual direct acquisition has individual receipts.

Selected leads compared against familiar sources:
- Human QKI isoforms (PMC13234107): original purpose glial precursor engineering/nerve repair, discovered via RNA-binding/splicing terms, not target-name search. Newly inspected primary text already exposes PMP22 variant directions (known, retrospective), human precursor rather than mature myelinating SC context. Needed new use: separate total RNA from isoform balance and compare event-wide splicing. No accession/full matrix in article; data availability says upon request; linked supplement is PDF only. Springer DNS fails, alternative EuropePMC archive HTTP500. Further legitimate public supplement route may clarify primers, but a full quantitative event analysis is currently blocked.
- FDFT1/cholesterol (PMC13042600): original purpose structural cholesterol versus IGF1 signaling in nerve regeneration; indirect nuclear-receptor/cholesterol query. Proposed new use: complete Flox-vs-cKO SC RNA matrix to test whether Pmp22 covaries with differentiation or sterol program. Archive acquired and inventoried; native data ZIP contains blot/microscopy/STR PDFs only, supplement DOCX contains figures/reagents/primers, no RNA matrix; data upon request. Do not infer target absence from selected figures. This concrete blocker is more consequential than its unfamiliarity.
- TSC1-mTOR-PLK (PMC6185760/GSE103957): original proliferation-to-myelination timing purpose; complete source FPKM files located at two GSM records, only one library/genotype, mm9 Cufflinks with required status audit. Gene-level comparison feasible but inferior for biological uncertainty to a replicated study; source methods also says Tsc1fl/+ mutant versus genotype/title cKO ambiguity. No target outcome yet inspected. Not rejected merely for n1; retain as descriptive potential cross-context test if needed.
- PRIDE PXD023091: current unlimited allowance removes historical size ceiling. Inventory shows four .msf search databases, not a ready replicate-channel matrix. SQLite inspection could be lawful, but HEK293 tagged interaction/selection and no endogenous amount endpoint limit discriminatory value. Not the best next acquisition relative to matched RNA/protein.

An independent mechanistic lead from mTOR discovery is PMC11014456, 'Neddylation orchestrates the complex transcriptional and posttranscriptional program that drives Schwann cell myelination.' It may supply orthogonal RNA/protein measurements, unlike the familiar ISR unpaired footprints. Original purpose protein modification in myelination; proposed new use is broad RNA/protein concordance plus PMP22-specific departure, with sample mapping and assay normalization as prerequisites. No target outcomes from this source inspected yet. Inspect primary methods/accessions alongside replicated Raptor injury (PMC5956991) and dual-function developmental mTOR (PMC5589416) before choosing matrices. Target-exposing source text makes any affected source reanalysis retrospective; an independent outcome test must be sealed later if metadata permits.

The choice now is not to deepen n1 TSC1 just because its file is convenient. Prioritize potential matched orthogonal endpoints and replicated upstream context interaction. Save rejection evidence and proceed with feasible analyses; no novel mechanism implied by source discovery.
